# Canonical Workflow Templates

RULE: Per-repo GitHub Actions workflows (semver-agent, request-major-bump, staging-lock-check, update-dependency-version, major-bump-issue-handler) are managed as canonical templates in `unified-trading-pm/scripts/workflow-templates/`. Never edit the per-repo copies directly.

WHY: 70 repos share these workflows. Editing one copy creates drift. The rollout scripts ensure all repos stay in sync with PM's canonical version.

DO: Edit the template in PM → run the rollout script → force-sync to remote.
DO: Use `${{ github.repository_owner }}` instead of hardcoded org names.
DO: Use `exit 1` with `::error::` annotations on critical operations (issue creation, Telegram, version bumps).
DO: For semver-agent, use `__REPO_NAME__` and `__SOURCE_DIR__` placeholders in the template.

NEVER: Edit `.github/workflows/semver-agent.yml` or other templated workflows in a per-repo directory.
NEVER: Use `|| true` or `|| echo ""` to silence critical workflow failures.
NEVER: Hardcode `IggyIkenna` or any org name — always use `github.repository_owner`.

## Rollout Commands
- Generic workflows: `bash unified-trading-pm/scripts/propagation/rollout-workflow-templates.sh`
- Semver agent: `bash unified-trading-pm/scripts/propagation/rollout-semver-agent.sh`
- Single repo: add `--repo <name>` flag
- Dry run: add `--dry-run` flag
